@startuml
left to right direction
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor white
  BorderColor black
}
skinparam ArrowColor black
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.2
title WF-2  Detection Engine Flow (updated 2026-10-05)

rectangle "Core App" as sys_1 {
  rectangle "Verify credentials" as event
  rectangle "Risk gate\npre-token-check" as gate
  rectangle "Revoke / require MFA" as lock
}

rectangle "core-db" as sys_2 {
  rectangle "login_attempts\n(no outbox rows yet)" as outbox
}

rectangle "Detection Engine" as sys_4 {
  rectangle "HTTP event endpoint" as receive
  rectangle "pre-token-check handler" as ptc
  rectangle "Rule evaluation" as rules
  rectangle "Combine risk scores" as combine
  rectangle "Enforce action" as action
}

rectangle "detection-db" as sys_5 {
  rectangle "Pending login attempt" as attempt
  rectangle "Risk assessment and alert" as assess
  rectangle "Detection log trail" as dlog
}

rectangle "ML Service" as sys_6 {
  rectangle "ML anomaly score" as ml
}

' ---- Risk gate: synchronous, before any token exists (2026-10-05)
event --> gate : password valid\n<<flow>>
gate --> ptc : HTTP POST /internal/pre-token-check\n(timeout 3s)\n<<flow>>
ptc --> gate : {risk_level, require_mfa, degraded}\n<<flow>>
note bottom of gate
  FAIL OPEN: error / timeout / degraded
  -> allow login, log warning.
  Only high/critical hold the token.
end note

' ---- Login event: direct HTTP, not via outbox
event --> outbox : INSERT login_attempts\n<<flow>>
outbox --> receive : HTTP POST /internal/login-events\n<<flow>>

' ---- Detection Engine receives
receive --> attempt : idempotent insert\n<<flow>>

' ---- Scoring
attempt --> rules : await process_attempt()\n<<flow>>
rules --> dlog : INSERT detection_logs\n(stage=rule_evaluation)\n<<flow>>

' ---- ML call
rules --> ml : HTTP score request\n<<flow>>
ml --> combine : anomaly score\n<<flow>>
rules --> combine : rule score\n<<flow>>

' ---- Risk assessment + alert decision
combine --> assess : INSERT risk_assessment\n+ alert\n<<flow>>
combine --> dlog : INSERT detection_logs\n(stage=scoring)\n<<flow>>

' ---- Action back to Core App, AFTER commit
assess --> action : risk_level in (high, critical)\n<<flow>>
action --> lock : POST /api/v1/internal/actions\nREQUIRE_MFA | REVOKE_SESSIONS\n<<flow>>

legend bottom
  The login response IS now dependent on the risk gate (2026-10-05):
  high/critical hold the token until MFA. low/medium issue it immediately.
  Scoring still runs inside the login-events request handler (await),
  so "background pipeline" no longer describes the current code.
  rule_score = min(1.0, SUM(score x weight) / SUM(weight of enabled rules))
  Risk formula: combined = 0.4 x rule_score + 0.6 x ml_score
  Fallback when ML is down or times out (>5s): combined = rule_score
  Outbox pattern is STILL NOT IMPLEMENTED - login events are sent directly.
  See DECISIONS-DETECTION-v3.3.md sections 10, 11, 12.
endlegend
@enduml
